    "updated_at": "2017-08-13T20:19:55Z",
    "body": "To me unreasonable starts when I have to call the API to see if it works. Getters don't work in older webkits that still haunt Android in large numbers, so you cannot use them, because they throw SyntaxErrors which is the worst thing that can happen to feature detection code.\r\n\r\nI think ergonomics should be a consideration in API design. Here it certainly wasn't and, again, it is a special case because the API change was not backwards compatible.\r\n",
